{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954375-followers-linked-to-birthrights","id":954375,"title":"Followers Linked to Birthrights?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T07:47:54-07:00","id":954375,"title":"Followers Linked to Birthrights?","content":"I've been confused about how followers linked to Birthrights work, exactly. Since most of the followers cost several dots to purchase, and yet a Relic can't be over 5 dots, I wasn't sure if the cost of the follower is connected with the cost of the relic.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, if a 4 dot guide was connected with a 1 dot relic, would that make the relic cost 5 dots, or does it merely serve as a conduit through which to summon them?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking because I've been curious to try out a character who focuses on building an army of servitors, but I don't know if that's possible to do without cladding him head to toe in relics, or if I can just use a <i>one and done</i> type of deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:25:38-07:00","id":954435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954375-followers-linked-to-birthrights#post954375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been confused about how followers linked to Birthrights work, exactly. Since most of the followers cost several dots to purchase, and yet a Relic can't be over 5 dots, I wasn't sure if the cost of the follower is connected with the cost of the relic.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, if a 4 dot guide was connected with a 1 dot relic, would that make the relic cost 5 dots, or does it merely serve as a conduit through which to summon them?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking because I've been curious to try out a character who focuses on building an army of servitors, but I don't know if that's possible to do without cladding him head to toe in relics, or if I can just use a <i>one and done</i> type of deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, Companion page 151 talks about Relic pricing, saying that it costs 1 Dot to gain the ability to link with one of your other Birthrights, spending one Legend point to acctivate this power. So, it's not just a One and Done situation. It, however, doesn't count towards the total cost of the original Birthright. If your ST is comfortable working outside of RAW, you might be able to alter the summoning power, bumping the cost in some areas. You could increase the Dot value of the power, increase the Legend cost, have a Legend cost per Follower group summoned, and if you then want to reduce these costs, have the summoning either take ten minutes, or have the Followers not arrive for ten minutes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:44:01-07:00","id":954446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954375-followers-linked-to-birthrights?p=954435#post954435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> have a Legend cost per Follower group summoned, and if you then want to reduce these costs, have the summoning either take ten minutes, or have the Followers not arrive for ten minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was hoping for, yes. Have multiple followers tied to the relic, but he has to pay for each group he uses. As for not arriving for a while, the relic I had planned is rather cumbersome to be lugging around in public all day, so they keep it stored away when they don't have immediate need for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}